WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.412 --> 00:00:16.121
"Don't fret," Wyssa said.

2
00:00:16.141 --> 00:00:21.265
"I learned magic in a world nearly as devoid of natural magic as this one."

3
00:00:22.205 --> 00:00:23.466
"Really?" Gliss said.

4
00:00:23.486 --> 00:00:25.027
"You can get us home?"

5
00:00:25.047 --> 00:00:28.189
"I know some tricks," Wyssa said.

6
00:00:28.209 --> 00:00:31.732
"First we need to find a spice market."

7
00:00:33.552 --> 00:00:41.298
She led them in and out of several shops, gathering mysterious ingredients— a strong-smelling powder, some dried leaves,

8
00:00:41.779 --> 00:00:43.200
a ceramic bowl, and more.

9
00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:48.003
After a while Zann noticed that they were attracting more and more attention.

10
00:00:48.884 --> 00:00:49.765
Perda noticed too.

11
00:00:49.785 --> 00:00:52.967
"People are staring at us," she whispered.

12
00:00:52.987 --> 00:00:56.910
"I think they're staring at Zing," Darb said, sounding worried.

13
00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:59.312
"What if someone else tries to grab him?"

14
00:01:00.604 --> 00:01:03.146
"Or what if the man who took Zing finds us?"

15
00:01:03.486 --> 00:01:04.026
Zann said.

16
00:01:04.046 --> 00:01:06.447
"He seemed really angry."

17
00:01:07.508 --> 00:01:10.369
He felt nervous as Wyssa led the way back to the wormhole.

18
00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:13.211
They were pretty close to the young man's shop.

19
00:01:13.771 --> 00:01:14.672
What if he spotted them?

20
00:01:17.293 --> 00:01:18.694
"Do you think this will work?"

21
00:01:19.554 --> 00:01:24.017
Gliss whispered as Wyssa started mixing ingredients and muttering spells under her breath.

22
00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:26.138
Zann shrugged.

23
00:01:26.598 --> 00:01:28.059
He knew that Wyssa was powerful.

24
00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:31.982
After all, she'd rescued him and Perda from that scatter beast.

25
00:01:32.843 --> 00:01:38.708
Then again, Zann couldn't help thinking about another time when Wyssa had lost control of a scatter beast.

26
00:01:39.748 --> 00:01:42.531
Maybe she wasn't quite as powerful as she let on.

27
00:01:43.792 --> 00:01:45.994
A little boy came toward them, kicking a ball.

28
00:01:46.014 --> 00:01:48.976
"Hi," he said, staring at Zing.

29
00:01:49.416 --> 00:01:50.017
"What's that?"

30
00:01:51.198 --> 00:01:53.560
Zann and his friends exchanged a cautious look.

31
00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:56.903
"Um, what does he look like?"

32
00:01:57.243 --> 00:01:58.124
Perda asked the boy.

33
00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:01.133
"He looks like a dragon," the boy said.

34
00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:03.073
"But dragons aren't real.

35
00:02:03.393 --> 00:02:04.434
My daddy said so."

36
00:02:05.314 --> 00:02:06.474
Zann glanced at Wyssa.

37
00:02:07.194 --> 00:02:10.955
She'd finished mixing and was stepping toward the spot where the wormhole should be.

38
00:02:10.975 --> 00:02:14.476
"Excuse us," Zann told the little boy.

39
00:02:14.496 --> 00:02:16.177
"We're kind of busy."

40
00:02:17.217 --> 00:02:19.618
The boy ignored him, stepping closer to Zing.

41
00:02:19.638 --> 00:02:23.279
"There's no such thing as dragons," he insisted.

42
00:02:23.299 --> 00:02:24.579
"So what is he?"

43
00:02:25.599 --> 00:02:27.820
Zann was so anxious that he lost his patience.

44
00:02:28.808 --> 00:02:33.169
"There might not be dragons in your world, but there are in ours," he snapped.

45
00:02:33.189 --> 00:02:38.131
"We're trying to get home, and we're worried that a bad man might try to stop us.

46
00:02:38.971 --> 00:02:41.652
So we don't have time for questions, okay?"

47
00:02:42.772 --> 00:02:43.912
The boy took a step back.

48
00:02:44.512 --> 00:02:45.353
He didn't say anything.

49
00:02:45.373 --> 00:02:48.374
"That wasn't very nice," Darb whispered.

50
00:02:49.194 --> 00:02:49.934
Zann shrugged.

51
00:02:50.414 --> 00:02:53.035
He felt bad, but he tried not to worry about it.

52
00:02:54.055 --> 00:02:56.896
All he cared about was getting out of this no-magic world.

53
00:02:57.792 --> 00:03:00.093
Just then a shout came from across the street.

54
00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:01.574
"Oh no!"

55
00:03:01.974 --> 00:03:02.574
Perda hissed.

56
00:03:02.594 --> 00:03:04.595
"It's the guy who took Zing!"

57
00:03:05.875 --> 00:03:08.717
The young man raced toward them clutching a large net.

58
00:03:09.537 --> 00:03:11.318
Behind him were two other men.

59
00:03:11.738 --> 00:03:13.039
They didn't look friendly.

60
00:03:13.859 --> 00:03:14.999
Zann glanced at Wyssa.

61
00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:19.281
She was sprinkling her potion over the wormhole, which was starting to glow.

62
00:03:20.061 --> 00:03:21.802
But the men had almost reached them!

63
00:03:21.822 --> 00:03:24.263
"Hurry!" Gliss screamed.

64
00:03:24.283 --> 00:03:25.644
"They're coming!"

65
00:03:26.656 --> 00:03:29.078
She grabbed Darb and crowded toward the wormhole.

66
00:03:30.259 --> 00:03:31.961
Zann grabbed Zing and did the same.

67
00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:34.283
But it was opening so slowly.

68
00:03:35.283 --> 00:03:36.064
"Stop, thief!"

69
00:03:36.464 --> 00:03:37.305
the young man shouted.

70
00:03:37.325 --> 00:03:39.027
"That dragon is mine!

71
00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:42.870
I—whoa!" The little boy had kicked his ball.

72
00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:46.913
The man tripped over it and slammed facedown into the pavement.

73
00:03:47.714 --> 00:03:48.755
"Oh no!"

74
00:03:49.035 --> 00:03:52.198
the other men cried, but they were running too fast to stop.

75
00:03:53.058 --> 00:03:54.500
They fell on top of their friend.

76
00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:57.021
"The wormhole's open!"

77
00:03:57.261 --> 00:03:57.842
Perda cried.

78
00:03:57.862 --> 00:04:00.064
"Let's go," said Wyssa.

79
00:04:00.844 --> 00:04:04.067
Everyone held hands as Wyssa pulled the group into the wormhole.

80
00:04:04.948 --> 00:04:09.211
Zann barely had time to glance back at the little boy, who was grinning at the fallen men.

81
00:04:09.231 --> 00:04:10.832
"Thank you!"

82
00:04:11.233 --> 00:04:12.334
Zann shouted to the boy.

83
00:04:13.214 --> 00:04:13.895
The boy waved.

84
00:04:13.915 --> 00:04:15.076
"You're welcome!"

85
00:04:16.337 --> 00:04:18.819
Then Zann found himself back in the vortex.

86
00:04:18.839 --> 00:04:21.401
"Whew!" Perda exclaimed.

87
00:04:21.421 --> 00:04:25.004
"I've never been so glad to be in this crazy place."

88
00:04:26.108 --> 00:04:26.909
Gliss laughed.

89
00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:31.573
"Yeah. At least there's magic here!"

90
00:04:31.593 --> 00:04:35.095
"We'd better stop and rest," Wyssa said.

91
00:04:35.115 --> 00:04:39.239
"Being in a world without magic might have weakened our energy.

92
00:04:39.599 --> 00:04:42.441
And we'll need plenty to get safely back to Magica."

93
00:04:43.602 --> 00:04:45.184
She pulled them through another wormhole.

94
00:04:46.004 --> 00:04:48.726
This time there were no people or buildings in sight.

95
00:04:49.587 --> 00:04:55.212
A babbling brook weaved its way through a grove of purple-leaved trees waving in a soft breeze.

96
00:04:56.364 --> 00:04:59.666
"The magic here isn't particularly strong," Wyssa said.

97
00:04:59.686 --> 00:05:03.148
"But there's enough to conjure food and fresh clothes.

98
00:05:04.089 --> 00:05:07.471
Then you'd better sleep for a while."

99
00:05:07.491 --> 00:05:08.911
"Good idea."

100
00:05:09.312 --> 00:05:10.752
Gliss stifled a yawn.

101
00:05:10.772 --> 00:05:14.515
"I feel as if I haven't slept in days!"

102
00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:17.716
Soon they were all clothed and fed.

103
00:05:19.137 --> 00:05:23.480
Zann lay down beside his friends, his mind racing with questions and plans.

104
00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:26.602
Wyssa knew he wanted to search for his parents.

105
00:05:27.523 --> 00:05:29.504
How could he get away without her noticing?

106
00:05:30.445 --> 00:05:34.868
Before he could figure it out, his weariness overcame him and he drifted off to sleep.

107
00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:39.192
He woke some time later, his heart pounding.

108
00:05:40.153 --> 00:05:42.294
He'd just had a dream about his parents again.

109
00:05:43.255 --> 00:05:47.358
This one had been especially intense, though Zann couldn't remember much about it.

110
00:05:48.319 --> 00:05:52.042
Just that his father was trying to tell him something about Morb.

111
00:05:52.062 --> 00:05:54.244
"Weird," Zann muttered.

112
00:05:55.084 --> 00:05:57.945
He reached into his pocket and touched the message stone.

113
00:05:58.766 --> 00:05:59.406
It was warm.

114
00:05:59.886 --> 00:06:00.767
That was weird too.

115
00:06:00.787 --> 00:06:03.308
"Are you awake, boy?"

116
00:06:03.628 --> 00:06:04.668
Wyssa stepped into view.

117
00:06:04.688 --> 00:06:08.310
"Good. We shouldn't stay here much longer."

118
00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:09.891
"Why not?"

119
00:06:10.171 --> 00:06:10.751
Zann asked.

120
00:06:11.291 --> 00:06:12.852
"What world is this, anyway?"

121
00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:16.494
"It's my home world," Wyssa admitted.

122
00:06:16.514 --> 00:06:20.175
"I'm, er, not exactly welcome here anymore.

123
00:06:21.116 --> 00:06:25.390
Besides, I promised your grandfather I'd get you kids home as quickly as possible."

124
00:06:26.511 --> 00:06:28.352
"Boz?" Zann was startled.

125
00:06:28.372 --> 00:06:30.253
"What does he have to do with this?"

126
00:06:31.093 --> 00:06:35.175
Wyssa turned away without answering, nudging the others with her foot to wake them.

127
00:06:35.195 --> 00:06:37.276
"Time to go," she said.

128
00:06:37.296 --> 00:06:39.137
"Next stop, Magica."

129
00:06:39.978 --> 00:06:41.159
Zann's friends cheered.

130
00:06:41.739 --> 00:06:43.400
But Zann felt his heart sink.

131
00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:46.422
He should have sneaked away while the others were sleeping.

132
00:06:47.462 --> 00:06:49.603
How was he ever going to escape from Wyssa now?
